{"name":"Japanese Sable","hex":"#313739","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"sable","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A small carnivorous mammal of the Old World that resembles a weasel, Martes zibellina, from cold regions in Eurasia and the North Pacific islands, valued for its dark brown fur.","Any other marten, especially Martes americana (syn. Mustela americana)."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Sable-coloured, black.","In blazon, of the colour black."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sable"}],"entries":[{"title":"Sable","blocks":[{"text":"The sable is a species of marten, a small omnivorous mammal primarily inhabiting the forest environments of Russia, from the Ural Mountains throughout Siberia, and northern Mongolia. Its habitat also borders eastern Kazakhstan, China, North Korea, and Hokkaido, Japan."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ee/Sobol_bur.jpg/330px-Sobol_bur.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sable","wikidata":"Q26423"},{"title":"Sable (tincture)","blocks":[{"text":"In heraldry, sable is the tincture equivalent to black. It is one of the five dark tinctures called colours."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sable_(tincture)","wikidata":"Q936496"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fe/Sable_area.png/500px-Sable_area.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fe/Sable_area.png/500px-Sable_area.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASable_area.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/67/Sables.png/330px-Sables.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commo